  "content": {
    "id": "p22-q1-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "1",
    "prompt": "Solve the following absolute value equations for $x$.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 3,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p22-q1-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$|x+5|=3$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-2,-8$",
          "worked": "$x+5=3$ or $x+5=-3$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=3-5\\\\x&=-2\\end{align*}$$\n\nor\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=-3-5\\\\x&=-8\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 19
      },
      {
        "id": "p22-q1-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$|7-2x|=5$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=1,6$",
          "worked": "$7-2x=5$ or $7-2x=-5$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}-2x&=-2\\\\x&=1\\end{align*}$$\n\nor\n\n$$\\begin{align*}-2x&=-12\\\\x&=6\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 23
      },
      {
        "id": "p22-q1-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$|5-3x|=x+1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=1,3$",
          "worked": "Require $x+1\\geq0$, so $x\\geq-1$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}5-3x&=x+1\\\\4&=4x\\\\x&=1\\end{align*}$$\n\nor\n\n$$\\begin{align*}5-3x&=-(x+1)\\\\6&=2x\\\\x&=3\\end{align*}$$\n\nBoth satisfy the original equation.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p22-q1-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$|3x-4|=2x-5$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "No solution.",
          "worked": "Require $2x-5\\geq0$, so $x\\geq\\frac52$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}3x-4&=2x-5\\\\x&=-1\\end{align*}$$\n\nor\n\n$$\\begin{align*}3x-4&=-(2x-5)\\\\5x&=9\\\\x&=\\frac95\\end{align*}$$\n\nNeither candidate satisfies $x\\geq\\frac52$. There is no solution.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p22-q1-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$|3x-1|=3-x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=1,-1$",
          "worked": "Require $3-x\\geq0$, so $x\\leq3$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}3x-1&=3-x\\\\4x&=4\\\\x&=1\\end{align*}$$\n\nor\n\n$$\\begin{align*}3x-1&=-(3-x)\\\\2x&=-2\\\\x&=-1\\end{align*}$$\n\nBoth satisfy the original equation.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p22-q1-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$|3x-1|=|3-x|$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=1,-1$",
          "worked": "The arguments are equal or opposite.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}3x-1&=3-x\\\\4x&=4\\\\x&=1\\end{align*}$$\n\nor\n\n$$\\begin{align*}3x-1&=-(3-x)\\\\2x&=-2\\\\x&=-1\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 26
      },
      {
        "id": "p22-q1-g",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "g",
        "prompt": "$|x^2-5|=5x+9$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-1,7$\n\nSplit into the two possible signs and reject candidates with a negative right-hand side.",
          "worked": "Require $5x+9\\geq0$, so $x\\geq-\\frac95$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x^2-5&=5x+9\\\\x^2-5x-14&=0\\\\(x-7)(x+2)&=0\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe candidates are $7,-2$; reject $-2$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x^2-5&=-(5x+9)\\\\x^2+5x+4&=0\\\\(x+1)(x+4)&=0\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe candidates are $-1,-4$; reject $-4$. Substitution confirms $x=-1,7$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
        "id": "p22-q1-h",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "h",
        "prompt": "$\\displaystyle\\frac{1}{|x-1|}=5$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\frac65,\\frac45$",
          "worked": "$x\\neq1$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}|x-1|&=\\frac15\\\\x-1&=\\frac15\\quad\\text{or}\\quad x-1=-\\frac15\\\\x&=\\frac65\\quad\\text{or}\\quad x=\\frac45\\end{align*}$$\n\nBoth satisfy the original equation.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      }
    ]
  },
